00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:50.720
Design and Analysis of Algorithms.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:54.960
He received his PhD from the
University of Minnesota in 1996 and has been

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.650
at Purdue ever since that time.

00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:03.670
Mehmet Koyuturk received his PhD in 2006 in
computer science from Purdue University, and

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:06.680
received his
bachelor of science and his master's degree

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:11.030
from Bilkent University in electrical engineering
and computer

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:12.030
engineering.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:17.280
He's now currently a professor in the Department
of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.560
at
Case Western Reserve University, and holds

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:21.960
secondary appointment at the Center for Proteomics
and

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:25.189
Bioinformatics at Case Western School of Medicine.

00:01:25.189 --> 00:01:28.549
His research focuses on the analysis of biological
networks,

00:01:28.549 --> 00:01:32.119
system biology of complex diseases, and computational
genomics.

00:01:32.119 --> 00:01:34.340
Finally, he is also an associate editor for
the

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:38.460
IEEE ACM Transactions on Computational Biology
and Bioinformatics.

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:42.310
We're very excited to have them discussing
their work today.

